1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,870
In GTA 5, you broke line of sight,

2
00:00:02,870 --> 00:00:05,740
dodged the vision cones, and the cops forgot

3
00:00:05,740 --> 00:00:08,610
you existed. In GTA 6, that doesn't work

4
00:00:08,610 --> 00:00:11,481
anymore. The police remember what you look like,

5
00:00:11,481 --> 00:00:13,992
what you wear, and what you drive.

6
00:00:14,242 --> 00:00:16,729
So in this video: how the new wanted

7
00:00:16,729 --> 00:00:19,215
system works, what every star colour and icon

8
00:00:19,215 --> 00:00:21,702
means, how to clear each one, and how

9
00:00:21,702 --> 00:00:24,189
to escape even at high stars. Learn this

10
00:00:24,189 --> 00:00:26,675
and you'll stop losing your cash to the

11
00:00:26,675 --> 00:00:26,986
police.

12
00:00:27,236 --> 00:00:30,020
First, the most important rule. A crime has

13
00:00:30,020 --> 00:00:32,804
to be noticed. Someone needs to witness it,

14
00:00:32,804 --> 00:00:35,588
or an alarm needs to go off, before

15
00:00:35,588 --> 00:00:37,676
it gets reported to the police.

16
00:00:37,926 --> 00:00:40,600
That means preventing a response is much easier

17
00:00:40,600 --> 00:00:43,275
than escaping one. Rob a store and get

18
00:00:43,275 --> 00:00:45,949
out before anyone dials, and the police may

19
00:00:45,949 --> 00:00:47,286
never come at all.

20
00:00:47,536 --> 00:00:50,410
Timing helps too. Night can be safer for

21
00:00:50,410 --> 00:00:53,283
jobs, because the police react differently after dark.

22
00:00:53,283 --> 00:00:56,157
So plan bigger scores for the evening and

23
00:00:56,157 --> 00:00:58,312
keep daytime for the low-risk stuff.

24
00:00:58,562 --> 00:01:01,172
When they do come, there are six wanted

25
00:01:01,172 --> 00:01:03,782
stars, one more than GTA 5. More stars

26
00:01:03,782 --> 00:01:06,392
mean a tougher response, but the colour of

27
00:01:06,392 --> 00:01:09,002
the stars tells you something just as important.

28
00:01:09,252 --> 00:01:12,052
Hollow white stars mean a crime was reported,

29
00:01:12,052 --> 00:01:14,852
but the police have no description of you.

30
00:01:14,852 --> 00:01:17,652
That's your best moment: leave before they arrive.

31
00:01:17,902 --> 00:01:20,462
Solid white means they've identified you and can

32
00:01:20,462 --> 00:01:23,022
see you. Your job is to break line

33
00:01:23,022 --> 00:01:23,662
of sight.

34
00:01:23,912 --> 00:01:26,458
Flashing white means they've lost sight of you

35
00:01:26,458 --> 00:01:29,004
and are searching your last known spot. Stay

36
00:01:29,004 --> 00:01:31,232
hidden and keep moving away from it.

37
00:01:31,482 --> 00:01:33,889
And red means you've escaped, but the police

38
00:01:33,889 --> 00:01:36,296
are still searching the area with your description.

39
00:01:36,296 --> 00:01:38,703
You're not safe yet. You still need to

40
00:01:38,703 --> 00:01:39,906
clear what they know.

41
00:01:40,156 --> 00:01:42,754
Which brings us to the biggest change: heat

42
00:01:42,754 --> 00:01:45,352
icons. Under your stars, a row of red

43
00:01:45,352 --> 00:01:47,950
icons shows exactly what the police know about

44
00:01:47,950 --> 00:01:50,548
you. And each one has its own fix.

45
00:01:50,798 --> 00:01:53,914
The person icon is your face and physical

46
00:01:53,914 --> 00:01:57,029
description. Clear it with a mask, a hat,

47
00:01:57,029 --> 00:01:59,366
sunglasses, or even a new hairstyle.

48
00:01:59,616 --> 00:02:02,622
A new hairstyle is a clever one. It

49
00:02:02,622 --> 00:02:05,627
changes your description permanently, until the next crime,

50
00:02:05,627 --> 00:02:08,633
but remember it only changes your face, not

51
00:02:08,633 --> 00:02:09,384
your clothes.

52
00:02:09,634 --> 00:02:12,202
The clothes hanger is your outfit. That one

53
00:02:12,202 --> 00:02:14,770
needs a full change, head to toe. A

54
00:02:14,770 --> 00:02:17,338
cap alone clears your face, but the clothing

55
00:02:17,338 --> 00:02:19,906
icon stays until you change your whole outfit.

56
00:02:20,156 --> 00:02:22,708
You can change at any clothing store, or

57
00:02:22,708 --> 00:02:25,259
just call your personal vehicle and grab the

58
00:02:25,259 --> 00:02:27,811
spare outfit from the trunk. The trunk is

59
00:02:27,811 --> 00:02:30,044
faster, so always keep one in there.

60
00:02:30,294 --> 00:02:33,098
The car icon is the vehicle you used.

61
00:02:33,098 --> 00:02:35,903
Ditch it or switch cars. And avoid using

62
00:02:35,903 --> 00:02:38,707
the same getaway car for multiple robberies, because

63
00:02:38,707 --> 00:02:41,511
once it's identified, it'll bring the heat right

64
00:02:41,511 --> 00:02:41,862
back.

65
00:02:42,112 --> 00:02:44,773
The gun icon is the weapon they saw.

66
00:02:44,773 --> 00:02:47,433
Put it away, ideally in your trunk. Pistols

67
00:02:47,433 --> 00:02:50,094
can be holstered, long guns need to be

68
00:02:50,094 --> 00:02:52,754
stowed or dropped, and dropped weapons go back

69
00:02:52,754 --> 00:02:53,752
to your trunk.

70
00:02:54,002 --> 00:02:57,221
The camera icon means CCTV footage. Destroy the

71
00:02:57,221 --> 00:03:00,440
footage, which is usually in a store's back

72
00:03:00,440 --> 00:03:00,842
room.

73
00:03:01,092 --> 00:03:03,940
And the two-people icon means Jason and Lucia

74
00:03:03,940 --> 00:03:06,788
were seen together. The fix is to split

75
00:03:06,788 --> 00:03:07,500
them up.

76
00:03:07,750 --> 00:03:10,469
Here's the catch: each icon clears separately, and

77
00:03:10,469 --> 00:03:13,188
any single matching detail can still get you

78
00:03:13,188 --> 00:03:15,907
recognised. Clear four out of five and you

79
00:03:15,907 --> 00:03:18,286
can still get caught on the fifth.

80
00:03:18,536 --> 00:03:21,208
During a search, officers in the red zone

81
00:03:21,208 --> 00:03:23,880
look for your description. Walk back into it

82
00:03:23,880 --> 00:03:26,552
while you still match, and the chase restarts.

83
00:03:26,802 --> 00:03:29,656
The minimap doesn't show police or vision cones

84
00:03:29,656 --> 00:03:32,511
anymore, so open the full map during a

85
00:03:32,511 --> 00:03:35,365
search to see that red zone. And use

86
00:03:35,365 --> 00:03:37,506
Focus Mode, which reveals nearby police.

87
00:03:37,756 --> 00:03:40,665
Even after you escape, hot areas stay behind.

88
00:03:40,665 --> 00:03:43,574
They're region-specific, and hovering over one on the

89
00:03:43,574 --> 00:03:46,483
map shows the active star level. At six

90
00:03:46,483 --> 00:03:49,392
stars, the hot area can cover the whole

91
00:03:49,392 --> 00:03:49,756
map.

92
00:03:50,006 --> 00:03:52,874
The officers linger, so your options are to

93
00:03:52,874 --> 00:03:55,742
wait it out, change outfits, or split up.

94
00:03:55,992 --> 00:03:58,435
Splitting up is more powerful than it sounds.

95
00:03:58,435 --> 00:04:00,877
Switch to the other character, and the one

96
00:04:00,877 --> 00:04:03,320
carrying the heat can lie low while you

97
00:04:03,320 --> 00:04:05,763
carry on with the other. It's built into

98
00:04:05,763 --> 00:04:06,984
how the duo works.

99
00:04:07,234 --> 00:04:09,978
Now the pro move: prepare before the crime.

100
00:04:09,978 --> 00:04:12,723
Wear a hat and bandana during the job,

101
00:04:12,723 --> 00:04:15,467
then take them off afterwards. Keep a spare

102
00:04:15,467 --> 00:04:18,212
outfit in your trunk, because your personal vehicle

103
00:04:18,212 --> 00:04:18,898
carries them.

104
00:04:19,148 --> 00:04:22,120
Use older cars you can hotwire for crimes

105
00:04:22,120 --> 00:04:25,093
rather than luxury cars. Luxury cars have electronic

106
00:04:25,093 --> 00:04:28,065
keys that need cloning, and modern stolen cars

107
00:04:28,065 --> 00:04:29,180
may have trackers.

108
00:04:29,430 --> 00:04:32,286
Advanced trackers are especially bad. They notify the

109
00:04:32,286 --> 00:04:35,142
police when the car is stolen and report

110
00:04:35,142 --> 00:04:37,998
its location unless you're moving at high speed.

111
00:04:38,248 --> 00:04:41,215
And buy a suppressor early. Police respond to

112
00:04:41,215 --> 00:04:44,183
gunshot reports, so a suppressor buys you more

113
00:04:44,183 --> 00:04:46,408
time to loot before anyone arrives.

114
00:04:46,658 --> 00:04:49,450
Destroy the CCTV before you leave, not after.

115
00:04:49,450 --> 00:04:52,242
Once the footage is out, you're managing the

116
00:04:52,242 --> 00:04:55,034
camera icon in the middle of a chase.

117
00:04:55,284 --> 00:04:58,157
As your stars climb, helicopters and police dogs

118
00:04:58,157 --> 00:05:01,030
join in. And the police work as a

119
00:05:01,030 --> 00:05:03,903
team: they shout commands, flank you, and break

120
00:05:03,903 --> 00:05:04,980
in through doors.

121
00:05:05,230 --> 00:05:08,041
At three stars or more, escaping in a

122
00:05:08,041 --> 00:05:10,853
normal car is very hard. A fast motorbike

123
00:05:10,853 --> 00:05:13,664
works better, or going on foot through alleys

124
00:05:13,664 --> 00:05:15,070
where cars can't follow.

125
00:05:15,320 --> 00:05:18,052
But remember, if officers see where you went,

126
00:05:18,052 --> 00:05:20,785
they'll follow you, even onto a roof. Breaking

127
00:05:20,785 --> 00:05:23,517
line of sight only works if they really

128
00:05:23,517 --> 00:05:24,200
lose you.

129
00:05:24,450 --> 00:05:27,522
For chases, there's a non-lethal trick: shoot out

130
00:05:27,522 --> 00:05:30,594
one or two tyres and the pursuing cars

131
00:05:30,594 --> 00:05:33,666
spin out. Helicopters back off after taking enough

132
00:05:33,666 --> 00:05:34,050
shots.

133
00:05:34,300 --> 00:05:37,386
The police try non-lethal takedowns first. But fight

134
00:05:37,386 --> 00:05:39,700
back, and they will kill you.

135
00:05:39,950 --> 00:05:42,594
Your aim matters too. Head and heart hits

136
00:05:42,594 --> 00:05:45,238
kill, while joints and limbs only injure. A

137
00:05:45,238 --> 00:05:47,882
red hit marker means a kill, yellow means

138
00:05:47,882 --> 00:05:50,526
injured. If you want to stay professional, aim

139
00:05:50,526 --> 00:05:51,518
for the legs.

140
00:05:51,768 --> 00:05:54,291
And one more practical note: a store you've

141
00:05:54,291 --> 00:05:56,815
robbed closes for a while afterwards. So you

142
00:05:56,815 --> 00:05:59,338
can't just hit the same place again once

143
00:05:59,338 --> 00:06:00,600
the heat dies down.

144
00:06:00,850 --> 00:06:03,386
If it all goes wrong, you respawn after

145
00:06:03,386 --> 00:06:05,921
the Busted or Wasted screen. But the cash

146
00:06:05,921 --> 00:06:08,457
you're carrying can be lost, so bank your

147
00:06:08,457 --> 00:06:10,042
money before any risky job.

148
00:06:10,292 --> 00:06:12,842
And if you're carrying stash bags when you

149
00:06:12,842 --> 00:06:15,392
die, you lose those too. That's why passing

150
00:06:15,392 --> 00:06:17,941
the bags to your partner mid-chase is so

151
00:06:17,941 --> 00:06:18,260
useful.

152
00:06:18,510 --> 00:06:21,636
Finally, the system most people miss: your criminal

153
00:06:21,636 --> 00:06:24,762
profile. It tracks how you commit crimes over

154
00:06:24,762 --> 00:06:27,887
time, and Jason and Lucia each have their

155
00:06:27,887 --> 00:06:28,278
own.

156
00:06:28,528 --> 00:06:32,952
There are five levels: Professional, Hardened, Violent, Psycho,

157
00:06:32,952 --> 00:06:37,377
and Irredeemable. A ruthless profile means faster police

158
00:06:37,377 --> 00:06:41,248
calls, armed citizens, and more aggressive responses.

159
00:06:41,498 --> 00:06:44,904
At Psycho, you can't surrender to the police

160
00:06:44,904 --> 00:06:48,310
anymore. And Irredeemable is permanent. So if you

161
00:06:48,310 --> 00:06:51,717
want easier escapes, play like a professional: low

162
00:06:51,717 --> 00:06:52,994
violence, non-lethal takedowns.

163
00:06:53,244 --> 00:06:55,888
To be honest about the limits: a few

164
00:06:55,888 --> 00:06:58,531
things still aren't confirmed by the guides. Exactly

165
00:06:58,531 --> 00:07:01,175
which crimes trigger each star level, how long

166
00:07:01,175 --> 00:07:03,819
the police remember an outfit or a car,

167
00:07:03,819 --> 00:07:06,132
and exactly how the police dogs work.

168
00:07:06,382 --> 00:07:08,835
Nobody has pinned down how much cash you

169
00:07:08,835 --> 00:07:11,287
lose on a bust or a death either.

170
00:07:11,287 --> 00:07:13,740
So until someone does, assume the worst and

171
00:07:13,740 --> 00:07:15,886
bank everything before you start a fight.

172
00:07:16,136 --> 00:07:19,051
My advice is to practise on a low-security

173
00:07:19,051 --> 00:07:21,967
store. Get one star, then run the full

174
00:07:21,967 --> 00:07:24,882
routine: break line of sight, leave the zone,

175
00:07:24,882 --> 00:07:27,797
clear every icon. Once it's muscle memory, the

176
00:07:27,797 --> 00:07:29,984
big heists get much less scary.

177
00:07:30,234 --> 00:07:33,235
So here's the full escape routine. Break line

178
00:07:33,235 --> 00:07:36,237
of sight. Leave the red zone. Then clear

179
00:07:36,237 --> 00:07:39,238
every icon: new hat or mask, full outfit

180
00:07:39,238 --> 00:07:42,239
change, new car, gun away, footage destroyed, and

181
00:07:42,239 --> 00:07:44,490
split up if you're a duo.

182
00:07:44,740 --> 00:07:47,202
Do that and the heat actually goes away,

183
00:07:47,202 --> 00:07:49,664
instead of following you back to your next

184
00:07:49,664 --> 00:07:49,972
job.

185
00:07:50,222 --> 00:07:53,069
Three mistakes that get people caught. Mistake one:

186
00:07:53,069 --> 00:07:55,916
only putting on a hat. Your face is

187
00:07:55,916 --> 00:07:58,763
covered, but your clothes still match, so the

188
00:07:58,763 --> 00:08:00,542
hanger icon gives you away.

189
00:08:00,792 --> 00:08:03,626
Mistake two: driving the getaway car home. Once

190
00:08:03,626 --> 00:08:06,460
that car is identified, it's part of your

191
00:08:06,460 --> 00:08:09,294
heat. Ditch it, even if it's a nice

192
00:08:09,294 --> 00:08:09,648
one.

193
00:08:09,898 --> 00:08:12,505
Mistake three: walking back into the red zone

194
00:08:12,505 --> 00:08:15,113
too early. If you still match the description,

195
00:08:15,113 --> 00:08:17,720
the officers in that zone will recognise you

196
00:08:17,720 --> 00:08:20,002
and the chase starts all over again.

197
00:08:20,252 --> 00:08:22,711
Have you had a chase where the police

198
00:08:22,711 --> 00:08:25,169
found you anyway? Tell me what gave you

199
00:08:25,169 --> 00:08:27,628
away in the comments. And subscribe, because next

200
00:08:27,628 --> 00:08:30,087
we're digging into the hidden details and easter

201
00:08:30,087 --> 00:08:31,316
eggs in GTA 6.
